 not allowed in this environment; provider messaging has to go through OpenClaw’s native routing, not direct API requests.\n\nSo:\n- your PowerShell example is valid in general for Telegram\n- but I should not implement that path inside this tool/runtime\n- the correct fix is to use an OpenClaw-supported attachment/message send path for the saved image\n\nIf you want, I can help with one of these instead:\n1. adapt the tool to return the downloaded image path in the exact shape an OpenClaw attachment sender expects\n2. inspect local OpenClaw docs/config for the proper native image-send mechanism\n3. generate a standalone PowerShell script for you to run outside OpenClaw with your bot token/chat id","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0443d925e91ce8820169ba876080048191aa899c0768633e2c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":346,"output":289,"cacheRead":123392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":124027,"cost":{"input":0.0008650000000000001,"output":0.004335,"cacheRead":0.030847999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.036048}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773832021470}}
