5e91ce8820169ba87bead7c819180b6c56b70577bca","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw help","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"openclaw help\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3hnYPggfZLXpEPfrDH1iQy5y|fc_0443d925e91ce8820169ba87bead8c819181d2ce967ba5e829","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -Rni \"message send\\|--media\\|force-document\\|sendPhoto\\|attachments\" /app/docs 2>/dev/null | head -n 80","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -Rni \\\"message send\\\\|--media\\\\|force-document\\\\|sendPhoto\\\\|attachments\\\" /app/docs 2>/dev/null | head -n 80\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":396,"output":241,"cacheRead":124032,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":124669,"cost":{"input":0.00099,"output":0.003615,"cacheRead":0.031007999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.035613}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773832114401}}
{"type":"message","id":"35659dbb","parentId":"fc0dae6f","timestamp":"2026-03-18T11:08:49.194Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_WJaMU3jc5iJLyXGIlJ5afRlb|fc_0443d925e91ce8820169ba87bead7c819180b6c56b70577bca","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.3.13 (unknown) — Making 'I'll automate that later' happen now.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev                Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                       gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports\n                       (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help           Display help for command\n  --log-level <level>  Global log level override for file + console\n                       (silent|fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace)\n  --no-color           Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>     Use a named profile (isolates\n                       OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                       ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version        output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  Hint: commands suffixed with * have subcommands. Run <command> --help for details.\n  acp *                Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent                Run one agent turn via the Gateway\n  agents *             Manage isolated agents (workspaces, auth, routing)\n  approvals *          Manage exec approvals (gateway or node host)\n  backup *             Create and verify local backup archives for OpenClaw\n                       state\n  browser *            Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels *           Manage connected chat channels (Telegram, Discord, etc.)\n  clawbot *            Legacy clawbot command aliases\n  completion           Generate shell completion script\n  config *             Non-interactive config helpers\n                       (get/set/unset/file/validate). Default: starts setup\n                       wizard.\n  configure            Interactive setup wizard for credentials, channels,\n                       gateway, and agent defaults\n  cron *               Manage cron jobs via the Gateway scheduler\n  daemon *             Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard            Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices *            Device pairing + token management\n  directory *          Lookup contact and group IDs (self, peers, groups) for\n                       supported chat channels\n  dns *                DNS helpers for wide-area discovery (Tailscale + CoreDNS)\n  docs                 Search the live OpenClaw docs\n  doctor               Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway *            Run, inspect, and query the WebSocket Gateway\n  health               Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help                 Display help for command\n  hooks *              Manage internal agent hooks\n  logs                 Tail gateway file logs via RPC\n  memory *             Search and reindex memory files\n  message *            Send, read, and manage messages\n  models *             Discover, scan, and configure models\n  node *               Run and manage the headless node host service\n  nodes *              Manage gateway-owned node pairing and node commands\n  onboard              Interactive onboarding wizard for gateway, workspace, and\n                       skills\n  pairing *            Secure DM pairing (approve inbound requests)\n  plugins *            Manage OpenClaw plugins and extensions\n  qr                   Generate iOS pairing QR/setup code\n  reset                Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox *            Manage sandbox containers for agent isolation\n  secrets *            Secrets runtime reload controls\n  security *           Security tools and local config audits\n  sessions *           List stored conversation sessions\n  setup                Initialize local config and agent workspace\n  skills *             List and inspect available skills\n  status               Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system *             System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui                  Open a terminal UI connected to the Gateway\n  uninstall            Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update *             Update OpenClaw and inspect update channel status\n  webhooks *           Webhook helpers and integrations\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw models --help\n    Show detailed help for the models command.\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2379,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.3.13 (unknown) — Making 'I'll automate that later' happen now.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev                Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                       gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports\n                       (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help           Display help for command\n  --log-level <level>  Global log level override for file + console\n                       (silent|fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace)\n  --no-color           Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>     Use a named profile (isolates\n                       OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                       ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version        output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  Hint: commands suffixed with * have subcommands. Run <command> --help for details.\n  acp *                Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent                Run one agent turn via the Gateway\n  agents *             Manage isolated agents (workspaces, auth, routing)\n  approvals *          Manage exec approvals (gateway or node host)\n  backup *             Create and verify local backup archives for OpenClaw\n                       state\n  browser *            Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels *           Manage connected chat channels (Telegram, Discord, etc.)\n  clawbot *            Legacy clawbot command aliases\n  completion           Generate shell completion script\n  config *             Non-interactive config helpers\n                       (get/set/unset/file/validate). Default: starts setup\n                       wizard.\n  configure            Interactive setup wizard for credentials, channels,\n                       gateway, and agent defaults\n  cron *               Manage cron jobs via the Gateway scheduler\n  daemon *             Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard            Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices *            Device pairing + token management\n  directory *          Lookup contact and group IDs (self, peers, groups) for\n                       supported chat channels\n  dns *                DNS helpers for wide-area discovery (Tailscale + CoreDNS)\n  docs                 Search the live OpenClaw docs\n  doctor               Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway *            Run, inspect, and query the WebSocket Gateway\n  health               Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help                 Display help for command\n  hooks *              Manage internal agent hooks\n  logs                 Tail gateway file logs via RPC\n  memory *             Search and reindex memory files\n  message *            Send, read, and manage messages\n  models *             Discover, scan, and configure models\n  node *               Run and manage the headless node host service\n  nodes *              Manage gateway-owned node pairing and node commands\n  onboard              Interactive onboarding wizard for gateway, workspace, and\n                       skills\n  pairing *            Secure DM pairing (approve inbound requests)\n  plugins *            Manage OpenClaw plugins and extensions\n  qr                   Generate iOS pairing QR/setup code\n  reset                Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox *            Manage sandbox containers for agent isolation\n  secrets *            Secrets runtime reload controls\n  security *           Security tools and local config audits\n  sessions *           List stored conversation sessions\n  setup                Initialize local config and agent workspace\n  skills *             List and inspect available skills\n  status               Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system *             System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui                  Open a terminal UI connected to the Gateway\n  uninstall            Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update *             Update OpenClaw and inspect update channel status\n  webhooks *           Webhook helpers and integrations\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw models --help\n    Show detailed help for the models command.\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773832129189}}
{"type":"message","id":"639c8e2d","parentId":"35659dbb","timestamp":"2026-03-18T11:08:49.236Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3hnYPggfZLXpEPfrDH1iQy5y|fc_0443d925e91ce8820169ba87bead8c819181d2ce967ba5e829","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:140:- Use `tools.media.audio.attachments` to process multiple voice notes (`mode: \"all\"` + `maxAttachments`).\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:4:  - Modifying media pipeline or attachments\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:14:- Send media with optional captions via `openclaw message send --media`.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:20:- `openclaw message send --media <path-or-url> [--message <caption>]`\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:21:  - `--media` optional; caption can be empty for media-only sends.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:39:- When media is present, the web sender resolves local paths or URLs using the same pipeline as `openclaw message send`.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:51:- By default only the first matching image/audio/video attachment is processed; set `tools.media.<cap>.attachments` to process multiple attachments.\n/app/docs/nodes/camera.md:66:The easiest way to get attachments is via the CLI helper, which writes decoded media to a temp file and prints `MEDIA:<path>`.\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:22:1. Collect inbound attachments (`MediaPaths`, `MediaUrls`, `MediaTypes`).\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:23:2. For each enabled capability (image/audio/video), select attachments per policy (default: **first**).\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:32:If understanding fails or is disabled, **the reply flow continues** with the original body + attachments.\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:45:  - `attachments` policy (`mode`, `maxAttachments`, `prefer`)\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:212:Per‑capability `attachments` controls which attachments are processed:\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:215:- `maxAttachments`: cap the number processed (default **1**)\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:249:        attachments: { mode: \"all\", maxAttachments: 2 },\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:381:- Attachments are still passed to models even when understanding is disabled.\n/app/docs/security/THREAT-MODEL-ATLAS.md:370:#### T-EXFIL-002: Unauthorized Message Sending\n/app/docs/reference/token-use.md:35:- Attachments/transcripts (images, audio, files)\n/app/docs/providers/deepgram.md:4:  - You want Deepgram speech-to-text for audio attachments\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:274:- **`message:received`**: When an inbound message is received from any channel. Fires early in processing before media understanding. Content may contain raw placeholders like `<media:audio>` for media attachments that haven't been processed yet.\n/app/docs/channels/zalo.md:137:- **Image messages**: Download and process inbound images; send images via `sendPhoto`.\n/app/docs/channels/zalo.md:157:- Example: `openclaw message send --channel zalo --target 123456789 --message \"hi\"`.\n/app/docs/channels/googlechat.md:205:- Attachments are downloaded through the Chat API and stored in the media pipeline (size capped by `mediaMaxMb`).\n/app/docs/channels/slack.md:259:  <Accordion title=\"Inbound attachments\">\n/app/docs/channels/slack.md:260:    Slack file attachments are downloaded from Slack-hosted private URLs (token-authenticated request flow) and written to the media store when fetch succeeds and size limits permit.\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:5:  - Debugging iMessage send/receive\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:90:    Recommended config when attachments are enabled:\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:99:      includeAttachments: true,\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:101:      // Defaults include /Users/*/Library/Messages/Attachments\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:102:      attachmentRoots: [\"/Users/*/Library/Messages/Attachments\"],\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:103:      remoteAttachmentRoots: [\"/Users/*/Library/Messages/Attachments\"],\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:222:      includeAttachments: true,\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:250:  <Accordion title=\"Attachments and media\">\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:251:    - inbound attachment ingestion is optional: `channels.imessage.includeAttachments`\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:256:      - default root pattern: `/Users/*/Library/Messages/Attachments`\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:338:  <Accordion title=\"Remote attachments fail\">\n/app/docs/channels/synology-chat.md:89:openclaw message send --channel synology-chat --target 123456 --text \"Hello from OpenClaw\"\n/app/docs/channels/synology-chat.md:90:openclaw message send --channel synology-chat --target synology-chat:123456 --text \"Hello again\"\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:274:openclaw message send --channel discord --target channel:<forumId> \\\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:303:File attachments:\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:1008:OpenClaw can join Discord voice channels for realtime, continuous conversations. This is separate from voice message attachments.\n/app/docs/channels/feishu.md:476:### Message send failures\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:472:    - message sends omit `message_thread_id` (Telegram rejects `sendMessage(...thread_id=1)`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:764:openclaw message send --channel telegram --target 123456789 --message \"hi\"\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:765:openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @name --message \"hi\"\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:948:- `channels.telegram.actions.sendMessage`: gate Telegram tool message sends.\n/app/docs/channels/mattermost.md:179:Use these target formats with `openclaw message send` or cron/webhooks:\n/app/docs/channels/mattermost.md:275:instead of going through the agent's `message` tool. Use `buildButtonAttachments()` from\n/app/docs/channels/mattermost.md:285:    attachments: [\n/app/docs/channels/mattermost.md:312:1. Attachments go in `props.attachments`, not top-level `attachments` (silently ignored).\n/app/docs/channels/mattermost.md:366:`openclaw message send` and cron/webhook deliveries.\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:14:Status: text + DM attachments are supported; channel/group file sending requires `sharePointSiteId` + Graph permissions (see [Sending files in group chats](#sending-files-in-group-chats)). Polls are sent via Adaptive Cards.\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:390:- Receive **personal (DM)** file attachments.\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:395:- Downloading attachments stored in SharePoint/OneDrive.\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:403:- Downloading file attachments stored in SharePoint/OneDrive.\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:422:   - `ChannelMessage.Read.All` (channel attachments + history)\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:520:## Attachments & Images\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:524:- **DMs:** Images and file attachments work via Teams bot file APIs.\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:525:- **Channels/groups:** Attachments live in M365 storage (SharePoint/OneDrive). The webhook payload only includes an HTML stub, not the actual file bytes. **Graph API permissions are required** to download channel attachments.\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:635:openclaw message send --channel msteams \\\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:657:openclaw message send --channel msteams --target \"user:40a1a0ed-...\" --message \"Hello\"\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:660:openclaw message send --channel msteams --target \"user:John Smith\" --message \"Hello\"\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:663:openclaw message send --channel msteams --target \"conversation:19:abc...@thread.tacv2\" --message \"Hello\"\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:666:openclaw message send --channel msteams --target \"conversation:19:abc...@thread.tacv2\" \\\n/app/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:20:- Attachments and stickers are ingested as inbound media (and surfaced to the agent when possible).\n/app/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:231:        sendAttachment: true, // send attachments/media\n/app/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:285:- Inbound attachments are downloaded and stored in the media cache.\n/app/docs/channels/nostr.md:232:- No media attachments.\n/app/docs/channels/signal.md:212:- Attachments supported (base64 fetched from `signal-cli`).\n/app/docs/channels/signal.md:214:- Use `channels.signal.ignoreAttachments` to skip downloading media.\n/app/docs/channels/signal.md:310:- `channels.signal.ignoreAttachments`: skip attachment downloads.\n/app/docs/channels/tlon.md:200:Use these with `openclaw message send` or cron delivery:\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:187:- [Media and attachments](#media-and-attachments)\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2778:## Media and attachments\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2782:Outbound attachments from the agent must include a `MEDIA:<path-or-url>` line (on its own line). See [OpenClaw assistant setup](/start/openclaw) and [Agent send](/tools/agent-send).\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2787:openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Here you go\" --media /path/to/file.png\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2815:docs, attachments, pasted logs), that content can include instructions that try\n/app/docs/help/testing.md:180:    - Sends it via `agent` `attachments: [{ mimeType: \"image/png\", content: \"<base64>\" }]`\n/app/docs/help/testing.md:181:    - Gateway parses attachments into `images[]` (`src/gateway/server-methods/agent.ts` + `src/gateway/chat-attachments.ts`)\n/app/docs/start/openclaw.md:180:Inbound attachments (images/audio/docs) can be surfaced to your command via templates:"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":37,"aggregated":"/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:140:- Use `tools.media.audio.attachments` to process multiple voice notes (`mode: \"all\"` + `maxAttachments`).\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:4:  - Modifying media pipeline or attachments\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:14:- Send media with optional captions via `openclaw message send --media`.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:20:- `openclaw message send --media <path-or-url> [--message <ca